        "paragraph": "There are partial retirement obligations within the meaning of the German Partial Retirement Act (AltTZG) of 23 July 1996 according to the block model. The partial retirement phase begins at the earliest after reaching the age of 55. During the partial retirement phase, the monthly part-time net salary is usually topped up to 85% (or 83% for contracts concluded after 1 October 2012) of the notional monthly full-time salary less statutory deductions. The obligations were netted against the fair value of the corresponding plan assets. If the fair value of the plan assets exceeds the obligations, the excess assets are recognised under receivables and other assets.\nProvisions for obligations from long-term work accounts are measured on the basis of certain accounting assumptions. Longterm work accounts are set up for longer-term time off in lieu. The reduction takes the form of a leave of absence with continued payment of the current monthly salary. The obligations were netted against the fair value of the corresponding plan assets. If the fair value of the plan assets exceeds the obligations, the asset surplus is recognised under receivables and other assets.",
