        "paragraph": "The Supervisory Board's rules of procedure set an age limit for members. Their terms on the Supervisory Board automatically end at the end of the Annual General Meeting following the member's 75th birthday. Moreover, a general limit of twelve years has been set for membership of the Supervisory Board.\nThe Supervisory Board also places value on fostering diversity in appointments to the Executive Board. The members of the Executive Board have diverse qualifications and work experience, which contribute to their work. In accordance with the provisions of the German Stock Corporation Act (AktG) and the German Corporate Governance Code (GCGC), in 2017 the Supervisory Board set a target quota of 25% for female members of the Executive Board, to be achieved by June 30, 2022. This target had not been achieved by this date because the existing appoint-\nments of four men to the Executive Board extended beyond this time horizon. Following the decision by Reiner Winkler to step down and the appointment of Dr. Silke Maurer as a member of the Executive Board with responsibility for OEM Operations and Chief Operating Officer (COO) of MTU with effect from February 1, 2023, the target of 25% female members was achieved; the Executive Board still comprises four members. The Supervisory Board has appointed Dr. Silke Maurer to the company's Executive Board for a three-year term of office.",
        "classification": "ESG",
        "report_name": "MTU_Aero_Engines_AG.pdf"
