        "paragraph": "For the financial year 2023, POLYTEC GROUP's total CapEx amounted to EUR 26,448k, of which EUR 4,041k (15.3%) were classified as taxonomy-eligible activities, with EUR 22,407k (84.7%) being non-eligible. Taxonomy-aligned CapEx, representing environmentally sustainable investments, totaled EUR 1,817k (6.9% of total CapEx), entirely classified as 'enabling' activities. These investments included: 'Manufacture of renewable energy technologies' (CCM 3.1) with EUR 73k (0.3%); 'Manufacture of batteries' (CCM 3.4) with EUR 0k (0.0%); 'Manufacture of other low carbon technologies' (CCM 3.6) with EUR 129k (0.5%); 'Manufacture of automotive and mobility components' (CCM 3.18) with EUR 415k (1.6%); 'Installation, maintenance and repair of energy efficiency equipment' (CCM 7.3) with EUR 948k (3.6%); 'Installation, maintenance and repair of charging stations for electric vehicles in buildings' (CCM 7.4) with EUR 159k (0.6%); and 'Installation, maintenance and repair of instruments and devices for measuring, regulation and controlling energy performance of buildings' (CCM 7.5) with EUR 93k (0.4%). For all these activities, a substantial contribution was made to Climate Change Mitigation (Y), while for Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Circular Economy, Pollution, and Biodiversity & Ecosystems, the contribution was marked as 'N/EL' (not eligible) or 'N' (for Climate Change Adaptation). Furthermore, all activities demonstrated compliance with all six 'Do-No-Significant-Harm' (DNSH) criteria (Y for all objectives) and met Minimum Safeguards (Y). The taxonomy-aligned CapEx for 2022 was 3.6%. Taxonomy-eligible but not environmentally sustainable CapEx amounted to EUR 2,225k (8.4% of total CapEx). This category included: 'Manufacture of renewable energy technologies' (CCM 3.1) with EUR 32k (0.1%); 'Manufacture of batteries' (CCM 3.4) with EUR 0k (0.0%); 'Manufacture of other low carbon technologies' (CCM 3.6) with EUR 1,204k (4.6%); and 'Urban, suburban and road p